Fixes the CI-only failure from PR #236's first run: 'dragging the last tab out
of a pane closes the emptied pane' failed 3/3 in CI, passed 5/5 locally even
under --workers=2.

Mechanism: the empty-strip append ran only from onDragOver. Playwright's drag
helper releases the button immediately after the final pointermove, so on a
loaded runner dragover never settled. handleTabDragEnd then found the tab still
in its source pane, fromPaneId === toPane.id, took the same-pane branch, and
the emptied pane was never dropped - hence 2 panes instead of 1.

This was a real product bug, not a test-timing artifact. Flicking a tab onto
strip space and releasing fast reproduces it by hand. Resisted the temptation to
paper over it with a waitForTimeout in the test helper.

Fix: appendedToStripSpace() is now shared by dragover and dragend. It is
idempotent - returns null when the tab is already last in the target pane - so
running it twice is a no-op.

How it was verified, because 'passes locally' proved nothing here: temporarily
disabled the dragover strip path so ONLY the dragend fallback could land the
append, and the three strip-append tests passed 9/9. That isolates the fallback
and reproduces the CI failure mode deterministically. Use that trick again
rather than guessing at timing.

